From a17a6240695078537fb850fe713b4db1c87b09a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Kacper=20Michaj=C5=82ow?= <kasper93@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:10:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] swresample: skip the rematrix stage when there are no samples
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When resampling first, a call that produced no output passed midbuf to
swri_rematrix() before it was ever allocated, and copied channels did a
memcpy() of zero bytes from NULL. Skip rematrixing zero samples, as the
output conversion already does.

Signed-off-by: Kacper Michajłow <kasper93@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit a17a6240695078537fb850fe713b4db1c87b09a3)
---
 libswresample/swresample.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libswresample/swresample.c b/libswresample/swresample.c
index d777efd802f3..6fe377f16c4a 100644
--- a/libswresample/swresample.c
+++ b/libswresample/swresample.c
@@ -654,10 +654,10 @@ static int swr_convert_internal(struct SwrContext *s, AudioData *out, int out_co
         if(postin != midbuf)
             if ((out_count = resample(s, midbuf, out_count, postin, in_count)) < 0)
                 return out_count;
-        if(midbuf != preout)
+        if(midbuf != preout && out_count)
             swri_rematrix(s, preout, midbuf, out_count, preout==out);
     }else{
-        if(postin != midbuf)
+        if(postin != midbuf && in_count)
             swri_rematrix(s, midbuf, postin, in_count, midbuf==out);
         if(midbuf != preout)
             if ((out_count = resample(s, preout, out_count, midbuf, in_count)) < 0)
